    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/steamed-cod-fillet-with-prawns",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/steamed-cod-fillet-with-prawns",
      "title": "Steamed cod fillet with prawns",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Steamed cod fillet with prawns</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/steamed-cod-fillet-with-prawns.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>Like many of the best dishes, this recipe came about by chance. I had leftover minced prawns (shrimp) in the fridge from making soup, so I threw them in with the fish I was steaming for lunch and this was the result. Tasty and quick, this is a real winner.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/steamed-cod-fillet-with-prawns.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-10-18T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pork-and-purple-broccoli-udon",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/pork-and-purple-broccoli-udon",
      "title": "Pork and purple broccoli udon",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Pork and purple broccoli udon</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/pork-and-purple-broccoli-udon.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>I have a special love for rice and noodles, all the types you can think of, and one of my favourites is b\u00e1nh canh noodles. These are quite difficult to source in the UK, but fortunately udon, which is readily available, has a very similar taste and chewy texture; like b\u00e1nh canh, it is delicious and super-easy to cook with. This versatile recipe is very quick to put together, and takes full advantage of that amazing udon texture by making sure the sauce clings on to every strand!</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/pork-and-purple-broccoli-udon.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-10-17T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/sticky-salmon-fillet-in-a-ginger-soy-glaze",
      "url": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/recipes/sticky-salmon-fillet-in-a-ginger-soy-glaze",
      "title": "Sticky salmon fillet in a ginger soy glaze",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Sticky salmon fillet in a ginger soy glaze</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/sticky-salmon-fillet-in-a-ginger-soy-glaze.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>When it comes to food, I\u2019m a huge fan of anything with \u2018sticky\u2019 in the title and I wanted to create that wonderful quality here, but in a slightly more subtle way, so that it could be enjoyed with a delicately flavoured ingredient like fish. This recipe combines my love for sticky sauce with wonderful salmon; hopefully you enjoy the combination as much as I do.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/sticky-salmon-fillet-in-a-ginger-soy-glaze.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-10-13T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
